From 19e56da4f2b62620d3f682127ce4fd303ffa604f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:35:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: Options > Graphics edits the Vita settings ([Vita] in
 Settings.ini) with a PGXP row; program cache loads without
 glBindAttribLocation

- t26 crashed at every start after the first: loading a saved program bound the attribute
  numbers (glBindAttribLocation) on a program with no shaders attached, and vitaGL's
  glBindAttribLocation reads the vertex shader (data abort, dump of 2026-10-28 23:16). The load
  path no longer binds them; the binary keeps them, and the attribute check rejects (compiles)
  one that lost them.
- The GRAPHICS menu parked since t20 (_staging/t20-menu, SHA-1 5465448...): pc_vitagfx reads
  Settings.ini's [Vita] section (RenderResolution, Widescreen, Smoothing, FrameRate, Renderer3D,
  and now PGXP), env.txt's THPS_* overriding; on the Vita Options > Graphics shows RENDER
  RESOLUTION, WIDESCREEN, SMOOTHING, FRAME RATE, 3D and PRECISE 3D (saved by APPLY, in effect
  after a restart, which it offers: "RESTART TO APPLY") with the distance and fog rows; the
  PC's window rows are hidden. PGXP comes from [Vita] PGXP (THPS_PGXP overrides). Boot line
  "[gfx] render ..., PGXP on|off (Settings.ini [Vita], then env.txt)".
