diff --git a/platform/pc/README.md b/platform/pc/README.md
index c8c661d..982a518 100644
--- a/platform/pc/README.md
+++ b/platform/pc/README.md
@@ -281,6 +281,15 @@ How the Vita build differs:
   depth from clip space instead of `gl_FragDepth`, and blending without dual-source outputs. It
   draws at 1x (320x240) and scales to the 960x544 screen. No shadows or MSAA.
   `THPS_GLES=1` builds it for Linux (with its own `THPS_BUILD_DIR`) to test it on a desktop.
+- Options > Graphics shows the Vita's own rows instead of the window, resolution, shadows,
+  antialiasing, VSync and game-files rows: RENDER RESOLUTION (512 X 240, 720 X 408, 960 X 544),
+  WIDESCREEN, SMOOTHING, FRAME RATE (60 or LOCKED 30) and 3D (NATIVE or PLAYSTATION), plus the
+  draw distance and fog rows. They are kept in Settings.ini's `[Vita]` section
+  (`RenderResolution = 960x544`, `Widescreen = On`, `Smoothing = On`, `FrameRate = 60`,
+  `Renderer3D = Native`: the defaults; an invalid value is the default) and read when the game
+  starts (`include/pc_vitagfx.h`), so a change takes effect after a restart (the menu offers
+  one). `THPS_VITA_RES=WxH`, `THPS_WIDESCREEN=0|1`, `THPS_FILTER=0|1`, `THPS_VITA_FPS=30|60` and
+  `THPS_RENDER3D=native|psx` override them. `[Video] Widescreen` follows `[Vita] Widescreen`.
 
